From: Emception maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] sysconfig: load explicit target data during cross-build

When a Windows interpreter bootstraps a POSIX-like Emscripten target, os.name
still selects the native Windows configuration. An explicit
_PYTHON_SYSCONFIGDATA_NAME is the cross-build contract for loading the target
configuration, so give it precedence without changing native initialization.
---
 Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py b/Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py
--- a/Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py
+++ b/Lib/sysconfig/__init__.py
@@ -499,5 +499,7 @@
-    if os.name == 'nt':
+    if "_PYTHON_SYSCONFIGDATA_NAME" in os.environ:
+        _init_posix(_CONFIG_VARS)
+    elif os.name == 'nt':
         _init_non_posix(_CONFIG_VARS)
         _CONFIG_VARS['VPATH'] = sys._vpath
-    if os.name == 'posix':
+    elif os.name == 'posix':
         _init_posix(_CONFIG_VARS)
